# Applies to the template SOURCES only -- this file sits above each template
# directory, so `nix flake init -t` never copies it into a project.
#
# A real project must commit its flake.lock. A template must not: the lock
# would be copied into every project initialised from it, pinning them all to
# whatever nixpkgs happened to be current the day the template was tested.
*/flake.lock

# Testing a template in place (direnv allow inside templates/<lang>/) leaves
# these behind. Each template's own .gitignore covers them for consumers; this
# covers them here.
*/.direnv/
*/result
